      "biography": {
        "type": "String",
        "label": "Biography",
        "value": "<p>The enormous Salinbader donkey is one of the largest breeds in the Old World. Originally from the former province of Salinbad just north of Salzenmund in Nordland, the breed is known for its distinctive shaggy coat that hangs in heavy locks. Usually chestnut coloured with a pale muzzle, they have long heads, long necks and particularly long ears that are so heavy they often fall flat. Affectionate, docile, and strong, they are mostly used for farm work and to breed mules, and local fables claim ancient tribesmen once rode them to war. Most Salinbaders are around 16 hands tall.</p>\n<p><strong>Commonly Owned By:</strong> Graverobber, Miner, Pedlar, Villager</p>"
      },
